<h1>John Kelly</h1>
<p>Candidate for Mayor, Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027</p>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/issues/" rel="nofollow noopener">John Kelly&#39;s campaign lists five issues, each with a written explanation. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Only Kelly: A city charter, a written constitution for city government. Kelly says Chicago is the only one of the 15 largest US cities without one.</p>
<p>Taxes: No new taxes of any kind, starting with property taxes. Johnson and Giannoulias want the wealthy to pay more; Nee will not rule out an increase.</p>
<p>Schools: Says CPS spends about 75 percent above the national average per student and should be judged on reading and math.</p>
<p>First cut: Says cutting 20 positions from the mayor&#39;s office would pay for five ambulances.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Property taxes: Freeze or lower them, with Holberg and Kitover. Hold the city&#39;s levy flat: Giannoulias. An increase is not off the table: Nee.</p>
<p>New taxes: No new taxes, with Kitover. Make the wealthy pay more: Johnson and Giannoulias. Cut taxes: Wilson. Savings first, before any new revenue: Quigley.</p>
<h2>the more perfect platform</h2>
<p><a href="https://johnkellyforchi.com/issues/" rel="nofollow noopener">Imported from johnkellyforchi.com</a></p>
